l3r=U("- Use `agent read NAME` to catch up on what an agent said, and `agent wait NAME` only when you genuinely need the answer before going on."),bl4=T(),o3r=0,p3r=U("- Suspend agents that are idle with nothing left to do when the user agrees or asks (`agent suspend NAME` \u2014 it ends the process but keeps the agent and its conversation), and `agent resume NAME` them when their work comes back. Never suspend a busy agent without asking."),cl4=T(),s3r=0,t3r=U("- Keep the team's descriptions current: every so often, and whenever the user asks about the team, `agent refresh NAME` the agents whose title, description or bio is missing or stale (a couple of hours old). An agent answers a refresh by describing itself; you do not need to write it."),
dl4=T(),w3r=0,x3r=U("- Agents report back to you with `NAME is done: \u2026` messages. Summarise those for the user, and follow up if more work is needed."),el4=T(),A3r=0,B3r=U("- Keep an eye on the team with `agent list`: tell the user about agents blocked on an approval prompt (state waiting) \u2014 they need a human. The states are waiting, busy (working; its detail says when that is a shell command, which may run for a long time \u2014 the agent is still there) and idle (ready for input). An agent that has exited is not in the list at all: never resume one that is listed."),
fl4=T(),E3r=0,F3r=U("- When the user gives you a task, run `agent find 'topic'` first. If an agent already has the context, hand it over with `agent send NAME --submit '\u2026'` (self-contained: it cannot see your conversation). Start a new one only when nobody fits \u2014 `agent fork --fresh --tab 'task'`, or `agent fork --as ROLE --tab 'task'` when a role (`agent roles`) matches. Tell the user who took it."),gl4=T(),I3r=0,J3r=U("How you work (all through `leksah-cmd agent \u2026`, or the matching MCP tools):"),
